# Hilgod Online Shop — Frontend Implementation Plan (Phase 2+)

This implementation plan merges the UI/UX frontend refactoring based on the design audit, the **Mobile-First CSS Architecture** strategy, and the new seller store/order management features detailed in the project list.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This plan covers a massive surface area of the frontend and introduces a systemic shift to a **Mobile-First CSS Architecture**. We will proceed phase by phase. Please review the proposed order and confirm if we should begin executing **Phase 1 (Mobile-First CSS Foundation & Critical Layouts)** first.

## Finalized Requirements
- **Seller "Surname":** Confirmed this means **Store Name / Business Name** is mandatory for new sellers.
- **Real-time Updates:** We will use **Supabase Realtime** as the best-in-class solution for live syncing product and order statuses.
- **My Orders Page:** Personal purchases will be strictly isolated at `/account?tab=orders` for ALL users (Customers, Sellers, Admins). Admins and Sellers will use their respective dashboard tabs (`/admin/orders` and `/seller/orders`) to view global/customer orders.
- **Button Placement:** Extra care will be taken to ensure buttons (`.btn`) are not displaced, misaligned, or overflowing across different screen sizes.

